title: The Coup
subtitle: An armed attempt against the government; PPS decides where it stands and what its organisations do.
new-page: true
tags: pl_event
face-image: img/polish/polish_event_coup.jpg
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && !!Q.polish_security_rules && PolishSecurity.coupDue(Q) !}
on-arrival: {!
// Event coup.attempt (Z — 1.03, the user's decisions 1B, 2B, 3B and 4A of 7 XI 2026; technical reference 16.4–16.8, 19.1; card
// catalogue 9.15): the stance of PPS, the call of its organisations and the outcome. One comparison of the forces with a hidden
// draw, as in the March on Berlin of the German original; no month is spent.
PolishSecurity.coupView(Q);
!}
go-to: f3 if pl_coup_step = "f3"; f4 if pl_coup_step = "f4"; f5 if pl_coup_step = "f5"; f10 if pl_coup_step = "f10"

@f3
new-page: true

= An attempt against the government

Units loyal to Józef Piłsudski march on the capital and demand that the government step down; the government refuses. [+ pl_coup_army +]

- @begin: Decide where PPS stands.

@begin
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupBegin(Q);
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@f4
new-page: true

= Where PPS stands

The factions of the party react as soon as we decide; a faction that is too angry may leave in part when the attempt is over.

- @support_pils
- @defend_legal
- @mediate

@support_pils
title: Support Piłsudski
subtitle: Factions: [+ pl_coup_support_pils_preview +]. The relation with Piłsudski improves at the end (+4, and +4 more for an executed share); the parties of the attacked cabinet the opposite.
choose-if: {! return PolishSecurity.coupStanceStatus(Q, 'support_pils').available !}
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupStance(Q, 'support_pils');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@defend_legal
title: Defend the legal government
subtitle: Factions: [+ pl_coup_defend_legal_preview +]. The relation with Piłsudski worsens at the end (−4, and −4 more for an executed share); the parties of the attacked cabinet the opposite.
choose-if: {! return PolishSecurity.coupStanceStatus(Q, 'defend_legal').available !}
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupStance(Q, 'defend_legal');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@mediate
title: Stay neutral
subtitle: Factions: [+ pl_coup_mediate_preview +]. No change of relations; the Milicja may only protect our own people.
choose-if: {! return PolishSecurity.coupStanceStatus(Q, 'mediate').available !}
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupStance(Q, 'mediate');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@f5
new-page: true

= The organisations of PPS

[+ pl_coup_militia_forecast +] [+ pl_coup_rail_forecast +] A strike of the railway workers holds back the trains with troops of the side we oppose; the Milicja fights on the side we support, or protects our own people if we stay neutral.

- @commit_none
- @commit_rail
- @commit_militia
- @commit_both

@commit_none
title: Do not engage our organisations
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupCommit(Q, 'none');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@commit_rail
title: Call the railway workers to strike
subtitle: A political strike of the railway workers; it costs the party nothing.
choose-if: {! return PolishSecurity.coupCommitStatus(Q, 'rail').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_coup_rail_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupCommit(Q, 'rail');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@commit_militia
title: Call the Milicja
subtitle: One task: to fight on the side we support, or, if we stay neutral, to protect our own people.
choose-if: {! return PolishSecurity.coupCommitStatus(Q, 'militia').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_coup_militia_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupCommit(Q, 'militia');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@commit_both
title: Call both the railway workers and the Milicja
choose-if: {! return PolishSecurity.coupCommitStatus(Q, 'both').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_coup_both_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupCommit(Q, 'both');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@f10
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
// 19.1: the resolved attempt ends the chapter; the report is recorded once.
PolishInstitutions.endChapterIfDue(Q);
!}

= The coup d’état: how it ended

**[+ pl_coup_outcome +].**

[+ pl_coup_story +]

[+ pl_coup_effects +]

- @polish_chapter_report: Continue to the report of the chapter.
